      <i class="fa-solid fa-key fa-2x text-primary me-3"></i>
      <h5 class="alert-heading fw-bold mb-0">YouTube API Key Needed</h5>
    </div>
    <p class="mb-3 small">To use the search feature, you need to add a YouTube Data API v3 key to your <code>.env</code> file. Don't worry, it's free and takes only a few minutes!</p>
    <ol class="small mb-0">
      <li>Visit the <a href="https://console.cloud.google.com/" target="_blank" class="fw-bold">Google Cloud Console</a>.</li>
      <li>Create a project and enable the <strong>YouTube Data API v3</strong>.</li>
      <li>Go to <strong>APIs &amp; Services &gt; Credentials</strong> to generate an API key.</li>
      <li>Add it to your <code>.env</code> file as <code>YOUTUBE_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY_HERE</code>.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <% } %>

  <!-- Tabs (Full Width) -->
  <ul class="nav custom-music-tabs" id="musicTab" role="tablist">
    <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
      <button class="nav-link active" id="yt-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#yt-panel" type="button" role="tab">
        <i class="fa-brands fa-youtube text-danger me-2"></i>YouTube Search Studio
      </button>
    </li>
    <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
      <button class="nav-link" id="focus-tab" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-bs-target="#focus-panel" type="button" role="tab">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-headphones text-success me-2"></i>Ambient Focus Tracks
      </button>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="tab-content" id="musicTabContent">

    <!-- ── YouTube Search Tab ── -->
    <div class="tab-pane fade show active" id="yt-panel" role="tabpanel">
      
      <!-- Search Toolbar (Matches Blog Toolbar Design) -->
      <div class="music-toolbar">
        <div class="music-search-wrap">
